Package: AmbientFilter
Title: Per-Cell-Type Ambient RNA Correction for Single-Cell RNA-seq
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: 
    person("Verchere Lab", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           email = "verchere@example.com")
Description: Removes ambient RNA contamination from single-cell RNA-seq data
    on a per-cell-type basis. Built on DropletUtils::removeAmbience(), this
    package extends the approach introduced by dRopt (CUAnschutzBDC) to all
    cell types in a dataset, with per-cell-type correction strength tuning,
    tissue-stratified background estimation, and diagnostic outputs. Designed
    for datasets with strong ambient signals (e.g. INS/TTR in human pancreatic
    islet scRNA-seq) that differentially contaminate non-expressing cell types
    such as macrophages, lymphocytes, and mast cells. Must be run upstream of
    subclustering.
